## Relationship to Regulatory Parallelism

DiMaggio & Powell explains *why* parallelism persists: when two regulators operate in different institutional fields with different isomorphic reference points, coordination does not emerge naturally. Each regulator's governance instruments reflect its own field's logic — the result is functionally equivalent mandates without cross-reference, precisely as observed in P3's empirical corpus.

